# Reference corpora and derived artifacts (~13 GB, all reproducible).
# raw/         -> src/method_evaluation/download_reference_data.py
# parallel/    -> build_parallel_corpus.py, sample_corpus.py
# transliterated/, cache/ -> transliterate_references.py (cache makes runs resumable)
data/reference/raw/
data/reference/parallel/
data/reference/transliterated/
data/reference/cache/

# Exception to the rule above: the Nisansa shard results ARE committed.
# They come from a rate-limited third-party endpoint that serves ~25k words
# before refusing, so they take several people several sessions to produce -
# not cheaply regenerable, and shared progress is the whole point. Manifest is
# committed too so teammates need no dataset download. ~20 MB total, no LFS.
!data/reference/nisansa_shards/
*.lock

# Per-item CER arrays: inputs to the significance tests, regenerated by
# run_evaluation.py. The aggregated results (metrics/significance/plots) are
# committed; these are ~68 MB of intermediates.
results/method_evaluation/per_item/

# Working notes
chat-session.txt
